91
00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:44.630
Exactly.

92
00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:47.330
So I started laughing like that.

93
00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:48.770
I said, what?

94
00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:50.230
I thought it was a joke.

95
00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.150
I thought I was getting punked somehow.

96
00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:53.310
I was like, what?

97
00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:58.310
And then Steve literally was taking a sip of water and almost spit it all over me.

98
00:03:58.430 --> 00:03:59.890
He started laughing so hard.

99
00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:03.450
And we looked at each other and I was like, what are you talking about?

100
00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:07.810
He turns to his assistant like, and she goes, the foot?

101
00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:10.590
And he goes, there was a foot that you guys had?

102
00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:11.930
Like a foot?

103
00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:15.450
I was like, oh my gosh.

104
00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:21.490
I said, you guys, you know how at Halloween you can go into Spencer's Gifts in the mall?

105
00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:22.730
Yeah, get like a foot that hangs out of the trunk.

106
00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:24.310
Get a foot that hangs out of the trunk.

107
00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:25.210
Ha, ha, ha.

108
00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.670
My mom got one of those.

109
00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:33.610
And instead of hanging it out of the trunk of the car, she put it by the bathroom door,

110
00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:35.810
