344
00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:33.600
No, it was Lester first, then Calvin, then Glenn.

345
00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:34.480
Okay.

346
00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:34.940
Hey.

347
00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:35.840
Which was crazy.

348
00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:36.960
I was like, another name tag?

349
00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:38.260
I'm like, yes.

350
00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:38.940
Who's?

351
00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:40.360
No one's keeping track.

352
00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:45.220
Well, I did see in the episode, the cover-up, that Daryl calls you Glenn.

353
00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:45.980
Correct.

354
00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:50.000
So your name is officially said in the series as Glenn.

355
00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:50.540
Correct.

356
00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:57.040
Well, we always like to start by asking people the same question, which is, how did you get

357
00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.460
your job on the office?

358
00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:03.740
And I read a tidbit that said it might have had something to do with the fact that you

359
00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:06.340
were certified to use a forklift in real life.

360
00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:06.840
Correct.

361
00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:07.740
Okay.

362
00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:08.840
Tell us the story.

363
00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:15.080
So I was pretty much a background actor on the office, as you know.

364
00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:21.960
But the reason how I got there was because I had a certification to drive a forklift and

365
00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:22.580
stuff like that.

366
00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:27.120
So my background, I was a supervisor at a corrugation plant in San Jose, California.

367
00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:32.840
And one morning, I told my boss, I'm putting in my two weeks notice.

368
00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:36.880
And that kind of ended right there that day because he was kind of mad at me.

369
00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:38.020
He said, you can leave now.

370
00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:39.640
And I was like, ooh, okay.

371
00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:44.060
Now, had you gotten the background job in the office when you gave the two weeks notice?

372
00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:46.160
I was still in the Bay Area at this time.

373
00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:46.640
Okay.

374
00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:51.280
And then what made you want to get into putting yourself out there for acting at all?

375
00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:56.660
So after I moved to L.A., I was in 24-hour fitness.

376
00:15:57.340 --> 00:15:57.580
Okay.

377
00:15:57.940 --> 00:16:00.640
And a guy told me, he was like, you should be on TV.

378
00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:02.940
You were just working out at the gym?

379
00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:03.200
Yeah, just working out.

380
00:16:03.340 --> 00:16:05.740
And a guy approached me and said, you should be on TV.

381
00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:08.860
And I was like, oh, okay.

382
00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:09.900
So how do you do that?

383
00:16:10.380 --> 00:16:14.320
So I just did some research and that's how I became on the show.

384
00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:19.880
So this is like an old Hollywood lore story where it's like Greta Garbo is like somewhere

385
00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:21.260
and they're like, you should be in the movie.

386
00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:21.720
Yeah.

387
00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:24.020
I call it right place at the right time.

388
00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:28.440
Well, was the office your first job then in the entertainment industry?

389
00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:31.660
The office was actually my third.

390
00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:32.360
Okay.

391
00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:33.580
What was your first job?

392
00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:38.900
I was doing other background stuff.

393
00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:42.360
So it was my first official booking.

394
00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:43.580
Was the office?

395
00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:44.480
Yeah, it was the office.

396
00:16:44.780 --> 00:16:45.140
Wow.

397
00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:45.980
Yes.

398
00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:48.020
That's what I said.

399
00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:48.420
Wow.

400
00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:51.280
I mean, had you seen the show before?

401
00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:52.480
Never, never seen the show.

402
00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:52.920
Okay.

403
00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:56.420
So will you share with us, like, what was your first day like on set?

404
00:16:56.520 --> 00:16:57.360
What episode was it?

405
00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:58.300
Will you paint us a picture?

406
00:16:58.560 --> 00:16:58.900
Okay.

407
00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:00.780
I'm going to take you guys way back.

408
00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:01.220
Okay.

409
00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:01.800
All right.

410
00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:08.500
So I remember back in, this is back in 2008, me and my wife were planning to get married.

411
00:17:09.160 --> 00:17:12.300
So what happened was I already got married in Florida.

412
00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:14.400
So we had booked our tickets.

413
00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:18.540
So I was called to work on an episode.

414
00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:23.960
And I told them, I said, well, I'll leave to go to Florida tonight because I'm getting married.

415
00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:25.440
I said, but you know what?

416
00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:29.700
I'm going to postpone that and just come shoot the episode.

417
00:17:30.130 --> 00:17:32.460
You postponed your wedding to come shoot the episode?

418
00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:32.940
Yes.

419
00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:35.840
So I postponed it and I went and shot the episode.

420
00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:39.560
And I was still background at this time on the show.

421
00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:43.920
And once we shot, I caught a red eye to Florida.

422
00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:51.780
And the day we got married was, we got married 8-8 at 8-0-8.

423
00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:52.420
Aw.

424
00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:53.060
2008.

425
00:17:53.060 --> 00:17:59.600
So the next day I get a call from Rainn Wilson and he said, we put together a little care

426
00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:01.040
package for you for your wedding.

427
00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:02.840
And I was like, what?

428
00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:05.580
Like, I was very ecstatic.

429
00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:08.180
I was like, you kidding me, right?

430
00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:12.160
So I want to say they sent me like three grand.

431
00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:13.480
What?

432
00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:14.240
Exactly.

433
00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:15.600
You know what?

434
00:18:15.760 --> 00:18:17.620
I actually am now remembering.

435
00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:18.720
Here's the thing.

436
00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:20.540
This is very early on.

437
00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:26.520
And I remember Rainn was like, hey, you guys, one of the warehouse workers is getting married.

438
00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:32.380
And now that you're saying this, I remember we all took up, like everyone chipped in, cast

439
00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:33.100
and crew.

440
00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:33.640
Yes.

441
00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:33.940
Correct.

442
00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:34.280
Yes.

443
00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:34.960
Correct.

444
00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:35.900
Cast and crew.

445
00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:37.960
Well, I remember we used to do that sometimes.

446
00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:38.480
We did.

447
00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:42.140
Actually, we did it quite often for different occasions in people's lives.

448
00:18:42.380 --> 00:18:42.440
Yeah.

449
00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:45.140
Graduations, baby showers, things like that.

450
00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:47.060
We would all chip in as cast and crew.

451
00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:47.520
Yeah.

452
00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:51.760
How that got to you.

453
00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:52.280
Yes.

454
00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:53.180
That is wonderful.

455
00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:54.660
Rainn sent that to me.

456
00:18:55.460 --> 00:19:02.420
And I was in tears in Florida on the beach because I didn't know that everyone cared like

457
00:19:02.420 --> 00:19:02.820
that.

458
00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:03.480
You know?

459
00:19:03.860 --> 00:19:04.800
So we got married.

460
00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:09.840
When me and my wife came back, I remember we went up to the office, went up to the set,

461
00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:11.500
and you guys were at lunchtime.

462
00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:13.560
And that's when I introduced my wife to everyone.

463
00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:19.040
I brought, like, a chocolate basket with the chocolate fruit, and I introduced my wife.

464
00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:22.500
And then we thanked you guys for that gift.

465
00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:26.940
And she was so embarrassed because I had her standing next to me, and I had to introduce

466
00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:27.820
her as my wife.

467
00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:29.460
It was so fun.

468
00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:30.060
It was amazing.

469
00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:39.060
And I think at that point in time, some of the writers didn't get a chance to add to it.

470
00:19:39.180 --> 00:19:39.640
They hadn't.

471
00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:41.140
Yeah, the writers hadn't chipped in, yeah.

472
00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:41.500
Yeah.

473
00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:47.020
So I get a call maybe a week later, and they wrote me in an episode.

474
00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:49.320
So I was like, wait a minute.

475
00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:53.520
Is this the Hollywood dream about to come true?

476
00:19:54.160 --> 00:19:54.600
Really?

477
00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:57.380
This is something really special about the office.

478
00:19:57.600 --> 00:20:02.640
I feel like it is a really special, you know, Jen and I talk about it for years now on this

479
00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:05.700
podcast that it was a really special group of people.

480
00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:10.400
And when you became a part of the office family, you were part of the office family.

481
00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:10.640
Correct.

482
00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:12.560
And we wanted to celebrate your accomplishments.

483
00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:17.440
We wanted to be with you if you were in hard times, you know, because there are people,

484
00:20:17.620 --> 00:20:19.380
cast and crew, who went through hard times.

485
00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:23.980
And we rallied around them as well, you know, financially, emotionally.

486
00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:26.900
It was just a special place to work.

487
00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:28.060
Yes, it was amazing.

488
00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:28.620
Positive.

489
00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:29.500
Yes.

490
00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:29.780
Yeah.

491
00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:30.300
Yes.

492
00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:32.840
Everyone is so amazing on that show.

493
00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:38.040
Well, when you first got your job and you're like, okay, I'm going to be a background player

494
00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:38.760
on this show.

495
00:20:39.740 --> 00:20:41.720
First of all, did you know that would recur?

496
00:20:42.060 --> 00:20:43.320
Did they say you might be back?

497
00:20:43.460 --> 00:20:43.620
Okay.

498
00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:48.780
So you're like, this is a one-off that now you are getting a gift for your wedding and

499
00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:51.080
you're a part of it and they're writing you in more episodes.

500
00:20:51.300 --> 00:20:51.480
Exactly.

501
00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:55.080
They were like, you know, they could keep asking you to come back.

502
00:20:55.240 --> 00:20:55.560
Okay.

503
00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:57.100
So I was like, okay.

504
00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:02.640
And in my head, as long as I keep doing great work, they'll ask me to come back.

505
00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:04.320
So that's what kept happening.

506
00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:05.800
They asked me to come back.

507
00:21:05.980 --> 00:21:07.280
Then they asked me to come back again.

508
00:21:07.880 --> 00:21:10.640
I didn't know that it was going to be a reoccurring part.

509
00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:13.120
I just thought it was like a one and done.

510
00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:13.740
Yeah.

511
00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:14.080
Yeah.

512
00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:17.760
Until my agent would call me, hey, they want you to come back.

513
00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:19.600
Hey, they want you to come back again.

514
00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:23.160
Well, in the warehouse, you're heavily featured.

515
00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:27.920
I mean, I was kind of going through your IMDb list of episodes.

516
